---
/**
 * How to reach a person, and what happens to what you send.
 *
 * This site publishes no email address, so this page invents none — a contact
 * page naming a mailbox that does not exist is worse than one with only a form.
 * The form is real, posts to this origin, and the page states the part people
 * do not expect: the address is also subscribed to the shop's mailing list.
 */
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteIcon from '../components/SiteIcon.astro';
import ProsePage from '../components/ProsePage.astro';
import ContactBlock from '../components/ContactBlock.astro';

const description =
  'Send a message to Glizzy Store. The form goes to a person, and your address is also added to the shop mailing list.';
---

<Layout title="Contact — Glizzy Store" description={description} scripts={false}>
  <SiteIcon />
  <ProsePage heading="Contact">
    <p>
      The form below is the way in. It is read by a person, usually within a few days. There is no
      queue, no ticket number and no auto-reply behind it.
    </p>

    <h2>Worth writing about</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>An order, or a question about one.</li>
      <li>Something on this site that is wrong. Corrections are welcome.</li>
      <li>A question about the object itself — what it is made of, how big it is, how it ships.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What happens to it</h2>
    <p>
      Your name, email address and message are stored by Netlify, which hosts this site, and read
      from there. Your email address is <strong>also added to the shop's mailing list</strong> as a
      subscribed customer in Shopify. That is worth knowing before you send it, and the
      <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a> sets out the whole of it.
    </p>
  </ProsePage>
  <ContactBlock />
</Layout>
